\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Stay, Master, stay upon this heavenly hill:
\par A little longer, let us linger still;
\par With all the mighty ones of old beside,
\par Near to the awful Presence still abide;
\par Before the throne of light we trembling stand,
\par And catch a glimpse into the spirit- land.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Stay, Master, stay ! We breathe a purer air;
\par This life is not the life that waits us there:
\par Thoughts, feelings, flashes, glimpses come and go;
\par We cannot speak them-nay, we do not know;
\par Wrapt in this cloud of light we seem to be
\par The thing we fain would grow- eternally.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. No, saith the Lord, the hour is past, we go;
\par Our home, our life, our duties lie below.
\par While here we kneel upon the mount of prayer,
\par The plough lies waiting in the furrow there.
\par Here we sought God that we might know His will;
\par There we must do it, serve Him, seek Him still.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. If man aspires to reach the throne of God,
\par O' er the dull plains of earth must lie the road:
\par He who best does his lowly duty here.
\par Shall mount the highest in a nobler sphere:
\par At God's own feet our spirits seek their rest,
\par And he is nearest Him who serves Him best.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

